# Walkthrough: Order Details Screen (v2.2)

This document provides a technical and functional overview of the Order Details interface within the LPG Delivery Management System.

## 1. Order Identification & Header
Each order selection triggers a contextual **Detail Panel** on the right side of the workspace.

*   **Order Number**: Displayed prominently in the top-left of the panel (e.g., `02/03-006`).
*   **Status Chip**: Indicates the current lifecycle state (Unassigned, Assigned, Dispatched, etc.).
*   **Customer Required By**: Shows the deadline requested by the customer, formatted for quick reading.

![Order Details Header and Panel Layout](file:///Users/admin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9cc2c976-1e1b-4644-a44b-f9a3ea44d3f3/order_details_assigned_1773686790476.png)

---

## 2. Items Ordered (PRODUCTS)
The **PRODUCTS** section provides a line-item breakdown of the order.

*   **Attributes**: Displays product name (shortened format), category, quantity, and individual subtotal.
*   **Scroll Logic**: The detail pane is independently scrollable to accommodate large bulk orders.
*   **Financials**: A summary subtotal is calculated at the bottom of the section.

![Items Ordered List](file:///Users/admin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9cc2c976-1e1b-4644-a44b-f9a3ea44d3f3/items_ordered_section_1773687200939.png)

---

## 3. Tracking & Driver App Integration
The **TRACKING** section utilizes a vertical timeline to show progression.

*   **Current State**: Indicated by a high-contrast dot (e.g., Green for Unassigned/Pending).
*   **Driver App Placeholders**: 
    *   **Dispatched**: Placeholder for when the driver starts the trip.
    *   **Delivered**: Placeholder for proof of delivery (POD) capture.
*   **Future Development**: Real-time GPS tracking details will be injected into this timeline once the Driver App is active.

![Tracking Timeline Placeholders](file:///Users/admin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9cc2c976-1e1b-4644-a44b-f9a3ea44d3f3/order_details_unassigned_1773687035139.png)

---

## 4. Operational Workflow: Assigning Orders
The interface adapts its action buttons based on the order's status.

### A. Unassigned State
*   **Function**: "Assign Route" button.
*   **Intended Action**: Redirect the user to correctly sequence the order in the trip planner.
*   **Target URL**: `http://localhost:3000/trips/new`

> [!NOTE]
> **Development Requirement:** The "Assign Route" button in the current UI is a visual placeholder. Implementation is required to link this button to the `/trips/new` route with the current order ID pre-selected.

### B. "Plan Trip" Destination
When the assignment flow is triggered, the user is moved to the **Plan Trip** workspace to select a Driver, Vehicle, and Route.

![Plan Trip Destination Workspace](file:///Users/admin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9cc2c976-1e1b-4644-a44b-f9a3ea44d3f3/plan_trip_view_1773689413889.png)

### C. Assigned State
Once an order is linked to a trip (e.g., `order=29`), the "Assign Route" button is replaced with management actions:
*   **Reschedule**: Moves the order back to confirm state or changes dates.
*   **Cancel Order**: Terminates the order lifecycle.
